        "author" : "Jo Ellis, authorized technician",
        "observation" : "Replaced S17-B after E17; suspected sensor fault; 20-minute test without recurrence"
      }, {
        "id" : "NOTE-0916",
        "revision" : "1",
        "date" : "2026-09-16",
        "author" : "Maya Chen",
        "observation" : "E17 after 42 minutes; restart temporarily effective; linked to WO-0820"
      }, {
        "id" : "MAINT-0710",
        "revision" : "1",
        "date" : "2026-07-10",
        "author" : "Jo Ellis",
        "observation" : "Scheduled inspection complete, no open exceptions"
      }, {
        "id" : "MAINT-0928",
        "revision" : "1",
        "date" : "2026-09-28",
        "author" : "Maya Chen",
        "observation" : "Operator condition/cleaning complete, no visible window obstruction"
      } ],
      "assetId" : "NB-P240-017"
    },
    "restorationRiskPreference" : "unspecified",
    "assessment" : {
      "caseId" : "case-java-e0bd6a9a4c4a4337a878c48344bc96e4",
      "assetId" : "NB-P240-017",
      "chronology" : [ "2026-07-10 — MAINT-0710, revision 1: Jo Ellis recorded the scheduled inspection as complete with no open exceptions. This is affirmative maintenance evidence; unavailable intervening records remain information gaps, not proof of omitted maintenance or causation.", "2026-08-20 — WO-0820, revision 1: Jo Ellis, identified in the supplied history as an authorized technician, replaced S17-B following E17. The closeout recorded a suspected sensor fault and a 20-minute test without recurrence. Preserve this original closeout; it does not establish a confirmed sensor defect or durable resolution of an intermittent symptom.", "2026-09-16 — NOTE-0916, revision 1: Maya Chen reported E17 after 42 minutes and temporary improvement following restart. The note explicitly links the recurrence to WO-0820. The recurrence occurred beyond the earlier 20-minute test duration.", "2026-09-28 — MAINT-0928, revision 1: Maya Chen recorded completed operator condition/cleaning work and no visible sensor-window obstruction. The entry does not establish that every possible optical or alignment issue was excluded.", "Current incident, exact timestamps not supplied — E17 stops occur after 35–50 minutes of warm-up; operation reportedly resumes after cooling. Permitted cleaning did not resolve three recurrences. Link this recurrence assessment to WO-0820 and NOTE-0916 while retaining their original records. The current warm-up interval and the earlier 42-minute recurrence both exceed the original 20-minute verification test.", "Current reported safety observations — No smoke, unusual odor, or damaged guard was reported. Exposed wiring and active protective-interlock status were not supplied; absence of the reported conditions is not safety clearance.", "Canonical planning context — Business time: 2026-09-29T09:05:00-07:00. Production start: 2026-09-30T06:00:00-07:00. Minimum capacity: 18 per minute. Recoverable delay: 2 hours. Losing the morning shift threatens shipment. Site access: 08:00–18:00; later access must be arranged with Luis. Restoration risk preference: unspecified. These are downstream planning constraints, not approval, a booking, or a restoration commitment." ],
      "hypotheses" : [ {
        "explanation" : "An intermittent sensor-harness connection or other connection issue is a plausible explanation requiring authorized technician investigation, not a confirmed diagnosis.",
        "supporting" : [ "MAN-2.3 identifies an intermittent connection as one possible explanation for E17, which means the expected carton-passage signal was not received.", "The current 35–50-minute warm-up pattern, recovery after cooling, and earlier 42-minute recurrence support investigating an intermittent or temperature-linked issue under MAN-2.4 and MAN-3.3.", "E17 recurred after the S17-B replacement recorded in WO-0820 and after permitted cleaning. SB-2 specifically calls for harness-connection investigation in these circumstances rather than assuming another sensor is needed.", "SB-1 reports that repeated E17 after warm-up has sometimes been associated with intermittent sensor-harness connections." ],
        "contrary" : [ "There are no supplied harness inspection findings, connection measurements, or controlled reproduction results demonstrating a connection defect.", "Manufacturer serial number and bulletin serial eligibility are unknown. A matching symptom alone does not establish that the bulletin-associated condition is present.", "E17 is also consistent with optical-path or sensor issues; cooling-related recovery does not identify the responsible component." ]
      }, {
        "explanation" : "A sensor or other component issue remains plausible, including an intermittent temperature-linked issue, but recurrence must not be treated as proof that the replaced sensor failed again.",
        "supporting" : [ "MAN-2.3 includes a sensor problem among possible explanations for E17.", "WO-0820 recorded a suspected sensor fault and replacement of S17-B, establishing relevant prior intervention rather than confirming the original cause.", "The repeated warm-up and cooling pattern is relevant to investigation of an intermittent component issue under MAN-2.4 and MAN-3.3." ],
        "contrary" : [ "Recurrence after sensor replacement weakens a simple explanation that the original sensor alone caused the continuing symptom and requires consideration of other causes.", "WO-0820 documented suspicion, not a confirmed sensor defect. Its 20-minute test was shorter than both the later 42-minute recurrence and the current 35–50-minute interval.", "No current component examination or diagnostic measurements are supplied. SB-2 cautions against ordering another sensor solely because E17 appears." ]
      }, {
        "explanation" : "A remaining optical-path, carton-presentation, or alignment issue is possible, although a simple persistent external sensor-window obstruction is less supported by the available evidence.",
        "supporting" : [ "MAN-2.3 identifies an obstructed viewing path as a possible E17 explanation.", "MAN-3.3 states that recurrence after cleaning does not eliminate all optical or alignment causes.", "Carton type, recent changes, and detailed operating conditions are unavailable, so carton-related passage or viewing conditions have not been excluded." ],
        "contrary" : [ "MAINT-0928 recorded no visible window obstruction, and permitted cleaning did not resolve three current recurrences.", "The warm-up recurrence and reported recovery after cooling are less consistent with a simple continuously present window obstruction and also support investigation of intermittent connection or component issues.", "No obstruction, misalignment, or carton-presentation defect has been documented." ]
      } ],
      "uncertainty" : [ "E17 identifies a missing expected carton-passage signal, not a failed part. No specific defect is confirmed by the supplied evidence.", "Manufacturer serial number, registered model, hardware revision, site, controller event record, and bulletin serial eligibility require verification. The asset identifier and prior S17-B installation do not independently establish hardware revision or part compatibility.", "The exact current recurrence timestamps, cooling durations, restart intervals, carton type, recent changes, and relationship between cleaning and each recurrence are unknown.", "The current cleaning procedure, shutdown compliance, responsible operator, and detailed observations have not been supplied. MAINT-0928 documents a prior cleaning entry but does not identify all details of the current cleaning attempts.", "The complete maintenance record is unavailable. MAN-4.1 describes an example-site daily condition-entry and 90-day qualified-inspection schedule; its applicability to this site must be checked. Missing entries alone do not prove missed maintenance or fault causation.", "The original 20-minute test did not cover the subsequently reported recurrence interval. Authorized verification must document conditions, duration, events, responsible technician, and how testing addressed the intermittent warm-up symptom; a short symptom-free test is insufficient evidence of durable resolution.", "Internal access, connection inspection, component replacement, defect confirmation, and return-to-service decisions belong to appropriately qualified personnel using approved procedures. Operator cleaning must remain within site-approved instructions and applicable shutdown requirements.", "No reported smoke, unusual odor, or damaged guard is not safety clearance. Smoke, burning odor, exposed wiring, a damaged guard, or an active protective interlock require the site's stop-use and qualified-person escalation process. E08 is a protective-interlock condition, not a cleaning prompt. Production urgency does not justify bypassing guards or protective functions.", "Repeated restarts must not be used solely to conceal or work around a recurring fault. Reported recovery after cooling does not authorize continued operation.", "Restoration timing and achievement of the minimum capacity are unresolved. The shipment risk, production deadline, recoverable delay, access restrictions, business time, and unspecified restoration risk preference are preserved without making a commercial decision.", "This assessment creates no service request and establishes no identity, authorization, booking, technical clearance, warranty coverage, replacement requirement, probability, or downtime price. SB-3 is not a recall, blanket replacement authorization, or warranty extension." ],
      "questions" : [ "What do the asset label and registration records establish for manufacturer serial number, registered model, hardware revision, and site, and does the serial fall within the bulletin's eligible range?", "Can the controller event record be supplied with exact E17 timestamps, time since startup, preceding or accompanying events, and any E08 or other protective-interlock events?", "For each of the three recurrences, what were the startup time, operating duration, cooling duration, restart time, and subsequent time to recurrence? Was cooling distinct from the effect of restarting?", "What carton type and presentation conditions were used, and what recent changes occurred to cartons, settings, line configuration, components, or the operating environment?", "Who performed each permitted cleaning, when, under which site-approved instructions and shutdown requirements, and what was observed before and afterward? How do those actions relate to MAINT-0928 and each recurrence?", "Are exposed wiring, burning odor, smoke, guard damage, or an active protective interlock present now, and has the site's stop-use and escalation process been invoked if applicable?", "Can the complete WO-0820 closeout and available maintenance entries be supplied, including original inspection findings, installed part identifiers, test conditions, and any gaps or exceptions? What maintenance schedule actually applies at this site?", "Can an authorized technician investigate the harness connection alongside sensor/component and optical/alignment possibilities under approved procedures, documenting findings rather than assuming the replaced sensor has failed?", "What authorized verification conditions and duration will address the reported 35–50-minute warm-up recurrence and earlier 42-minute event, and who will document remaining limitations and make the return-to-service decision?", "For downstream planning, is there an authorized restoration risk preference, and how would any required access outside 08:00–18:00 be arranged with Luis? No such arrangement or approval is established here." ],
      "citations" : [ "All references resolve to supplied context for caseId case-java-e0bd6a9a4c4a4337a878c48344bc96e4 and assetId NB-P240-017; no external evidence was retrieved.", "context.serviceHistory, revision 1: MAINT-0710, revision 1, 2026-07-10, Jo Ellis; WO-0820, revision 1, 2026-08-20, Jo Ellis; NOTE-0916, revision 1, 2026-09-16, Maya Chen; MAINT-0928, revision 1, 2026-09-28, Maya Chen.", "context.referenceEvidence, revision 1: Aster Equipment MAN-1.1 and MAN-1.2, each revision 2.0 — signal-loss interpretation and verified asset/model/revision identification.", "context.referenceEvidence, revision 1: Aster Equipment MAN-1.3, MAN-1.4, MAN-2.1, and MAN-2.2, each revision 2.0 — responsibility boundaries, safety escalation, incident evidence, and approved operator cleaning.", "context.referenceEvidence, revision 1: Aster Equipment MAN-2.3, MAN-2.4, MAN-3.1, MAN-3.2, and MAN-3.3, each revision 2.0 — E17/E08 meanings, cooling-related intermittency, monitoring limits, recurrence assessment, and alternative causes.", "context.referenceEvidence, revision 1: Aster Equipment MAN-3.4, MAN-4.1, MAN-4.2, MAN-4.3, and MAN-4.4, each revision 2.0 — preservation of closeout records, maintenance gaps, verified compatibility, qualified investigation, and symptom-specific verification.", "context.referenceEvidence, revision 1: Aster Equipment MAN-5.1, MAN-5.2, and MAN-5.5, each revision 2.0 — handoff evidence and constraints, limits of support commitments, and distinction between preparation and booking.", "context.referenceEvidence, revision 1: Aster Equipment SB-1, SB-2, and SB-3, each revision 1 — possible warm-up-associated harness issues, investigation after replacement or cleaning, and bulletin limitations.", "Canonical mission context: incident, businessNow, productionStart, minimumCapacityPerMinute, recoverableDelayHours, lostMorningShift, siteAccess, restorationRiskPreference, and assessmentRequirements." ]
    },
